[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3354669653","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3354669653","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3354669653,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H9DJV","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T04:10:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T04:10:46Z","body":"This text was recently added by @RolandMarchand in PR #109925, maybe he would like to give feedback on this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3354669653/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358116612","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3358116612","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3358116612,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IKMsE","user":{"login":"lazzy-cipher","id":90345171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMzQ1MTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90345171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher","html_url":"https://github.com/lazzy-cipher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T21:00:18Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T21:00:18Z","body":"> The way values are calculated should not be discouraged.\r\n\r\nErrors should be discouraged, and multiplying a velocity vector by `delta` twice is a significant physics calculation error. This happens when the user multiplies `velocity` by `delta` and then uses `move_and_slide()` which internally also multiplies the velocity by `delta`. Users should never do that, so it should be discouraged. We can argue about the specific language used, but I have not heard a single complaint about it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358116612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358646099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3358646099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3358646099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IMN9T","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T00:55:09Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T01:03:39Z","body":"@RolandMarchand This PR is saying the same thing as you're describing.\r\n\r\nThe original sentence discourages any form of `x * delta`. This PR changes it to noting that `px/s * delta` is a common mistake.\r\n\r\nThe key point is, `x * delta` is valid as long as `x` is in `px/s²`.\r\n\r\nThe root cause of the error lies in users not caring about the units of values. The original wording not only has false positives, but also encouraged the root error rather than resolving it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358646099/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3371433257","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3371433257","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3371433257,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7I8_0p","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-06T12:38:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T12:38:46Z","body":"> Note that there's a similar remark in [`move_and_slide`'s description](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102/files#diff-da01fd32c83dae8d0e0d34e887eb0c2fcf7f4528b5186225dfd8ef0b9b1799f6R144) that should probably be changed for consistency.\r\n\r\n@Mickeon I think that part is fine since it's just explaining why `move_and_slide()` should be called inside `_physics_process`: the method depends on the current physics delta internally.\r\n\r\n> This method should be used in [method Node._physics_process] (or in a method called by [method Node._physics_process]), as it uses the physics step's [code]delta[/code] value automatically in calculations. Otherwise, the simulation will run at an incorrect speed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3371433257/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3377770842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3377770842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3377770842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JVLFa","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-07T17:03:14Z","updated_at":"2025-10-07T17:03:14Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3377770842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3378230996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111102#issuecomment-3378230996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111102","id":3378230996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JW7bU","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-07T18:45:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-07T18:58:15Z","body":"I think the focus of his problem is not on the unit, but on clearly stating in the description of the move_and_slide method that the delta parameter has already been used for calculation. Similar to what the direction_to method explicitly states as returning a normalized vector. At present, this page(https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.html#move -and-slide) indicates this point, but the built-in document method description has not been updated synchronously.\r\nThis 'delta-related' thing only clearly stated in the description of the move_ond_comlide method like \"Moves the body along the vector motion. In order to be frame rate independent in Node._physics_process() or Node._process(), motion should be computed using delta\".\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3378230996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]